  },
  "note": "Election of the Omagh Urban Council, polled 21 May 1958; twelve Unionists and nine Nationalists were returned unopposed, the returning officer having rejected two late independent nominations (Ulster Herald, 10 May 1958, p. 7). The report names the Unionist and Nationalist panels but does not itemise them by ward; the Belfast News-Letter of 8 May 1958 confirms that no contest took place. Eakin, McKenzie and Stephens were the new Unionist members, Ferris the new Nationalist. Returned unopposed."
}
